should calibrate against the registry's honest base (the E3 note: 0/3 claims
held).
{% endif %}

## Candidates (ranked by likelihood, not ease of testing)

{{ candidates | tojson }}

Render the brief as an object:

- `question` — the funded question verbatim.
- `ranked_candidates` — the candidates in rank order, each with its citations
  rendered inline (an uncited candidate is dropped before rendering — say so by
  name if any were dropped).
- `total_budget_ask` — the sum across candidates, per enforced unit.
- `funding_options` — two or three coherent portfolios (for example: fund the
  top candidate only; fund the top two; fund one experiment plus one
  research-run resolution), each with its unit-stated cost.
- `agenda_promotion_note` — a reminder that the gate funds board cards only;
  promoting an agenda-registry candidate is the explicit act of filing it on
  the board with provenance.
- `refusal_path_note` — a reminder that a candidate refused at any downstream
  gate (falsifiability-admit, no-headroom, registry incompatibility) returns to
  the card as a cheap fossil with the gate name and reason; funding it is not a
  promise it survives.

The PI funds K. The funded number becomes the declared budget at
`experiment_propose`. End with the ask, in the PI's terms: which candidates,
at what spend, in which enforced units.